A PayPal payment notification needs follow-up.

Result: <%= @ipn_message.processing_result %>
Transaction ID: <%= @ipn_message.txn_id %>
Payment status: <%= @ipn_message.payment_status %>
Amount: <%= @ipn_message.mc_gross %> <%= @ipn_message.mc_currency %>
Invoice: <%= @ipn_message.invoice %>
Payer: <%= @ipn_message.first_name %> <%= @ipn_message.last_name %> (<%= @ipn_message.payer_email %>)
Received: <%= @ipn_message.created_at %>

<% case @ipn_message.processing_result %>
<% when "created_merch_size_unknown" %>
The race entry was created and paid, but the payment amount includes
merchandise and the merchandise size is not known. Please contact the racer
to confirm their size.
<% when "amount_mismatch" %>
The payment amount does not match the entry fee (with or without
merchandise), so no race entry was created. Please reconcile against the
PayPal account and create the entry manually if appropriate.
<% when "invoice_unrecognized" %>
The payment's invoice does not identify a race edition and racer, so no race
entry was created. Please reconcile against the PayPal account.
<% when "receiver_mismatch" %>
The payment was addressed to a different receiver email, so no race entry
was created. This may indicate a misconfigured button or a spoofing attempt.
<% end %>
